{"name":"Hydrangea","hex":"#768dc6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Hydrangea","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Hydrangeaceae – hydrangeas, most species of which are found in China."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Hydrangea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hydrangea","blocks":[{"text":"Hydrangea is a genus of more than 70 species of flowering plants native to Asia and the Americas. Hydrangea is also used as the common name for the genus; some are also often called hortensia. The genus was first described from Virginia in North America, but by far the greatest species diversity is in eastern Asia, notably China, Korea, and Japan. Most are shrubs 1–3 m tall, but some are small trees, and others lianas reaching up to 30 m (100 ft) by climbing up trees. They can be either deciduous or evergreen, though the widely cultivated temperate species are all deciduous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Hydrangea_arborescens_139866012.jpg/330px-Hydrangea_arborescens_139866012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrangea","wikidata":"Q155997"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Hydrangea_Flower_Color_Based_on_Soil_pH.jpg/500px-Hydrangea_Flower_Color_Based_on_Soil_pH.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Hydrangea_Flower_Color_Based_on_Soil_pH.jpg/500px-Hydrangea_Flower_Color_Based_on_Soil_pH.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hydrangea flower color changes based on the pH in soil. As the graph depicts, soil with a pH of 5.5 or lower will produce blue flowers, a pH of 6.5 or higher will produce pink hydrangeas, and soil in between 5.5 and 6.5 will have purple hydrangeas.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHydrangea_Flower_Color_Based_on_Soil_pH.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Hydrangea_paniculata_-_flower_view_01.jpg/500px-Hydrangea_paniculata_-_flower_view_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Hydrangea_paniculata_-_flower_view_01.jpg/500px-Hydrangea_paniculata_-_flower_view_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hydrangea paniculata","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHydrangea_paniculata_-_flower_view_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Hydrangea_knowltoni_as_Hydrangea_bendirei_USNM_P36979_img3.jpg/330px-Hydrangea_knowltoni_as_Hydrangea_bendirei_USNM_P36979_img3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Hydrangea_knowltoni_as_Hydrangea_bendirei_USNM_P36979_img3.jpg/330px-Hydrangea_knowltoni_as_Hydrangea_bendirei_USNM_P36979_img3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hydrangea knowltoni","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHydrangea_knowltoni_as_Hydrangea_bendirei_USNM_P36979_img3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Hortensiapink.JPG/120px-Hortensiapink.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Hortensiapink.JPG/250px-Hortensiapink.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Hortensiapink.JPG/120px-Hortensiapink.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHortensiapink.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/H